    {
      "id": "b000042",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 73,
      "end_line": 73,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000043",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 74,
      "end_line": 74,
      "raw": "SQL Server-based DB reproduction scripts are organized in [database/README.md](database/README.md). Executing in the order of `01_schema.sql`, `02_sample-data.sql`, `03_procedures.sql`, `04_reports.sql` allows checking tables, demonstration data, stored procedures, and report queries. Interview explanation answers are organized in [database/INTERVIEW_NOTES.md](database/INTERVIEW_NOTES.md). The application uses SQLite for local execution convenience, but SQL outputs are kept as SQL Server-based for interview demonstrations.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000044",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 75,
      "end_line": 75,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000045",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 76,
      "end_line": 76,
      "raw": "REST API detailed contracts are organized in [Docs/rest-api.md](Docs/rest-api.md). After server execution, Swagger UI is checked at `/swagger`.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000046",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 77,
      "end_line": 77,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000047",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 78,
      "end_line": 78,
      "raw": "Avalonia GUI preparation content is organized in [Docs/gui.md](Docs/gui.md). `OrderSystem.Desktop` includes a desktop shell, main window, and ViewModel structure to connect with REST API. The current GUI provides a mini shopping mall flow with a virtual product catalog, shopping cart, checkout, and shopping console logs, rather than a screen to directly inspect the API. The first project of the solution is placed in `OrderSystem.Desktop` so that the default execution entry point candidate becomes the GUI app.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000048",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 79,
      "end_line": 79,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
